---
id: acmi-medications
title: ACMI medications (Best et al, BMJ Medicine 2026)
description: The 88 anticholinergic medications scored by the Anticholinergic Medication Index (ACMI), bound to their SNOMED CT ingredient-level substance concepts from the NHS dm+d ingredient simple reference set (999000791000001109), for clincalc's acmi calculator. Isosorbide is listed in the primary source without specifying an ester; both mononitrate and dinitrate are included pending disambiguation - see the comment below.
terminology: SNOMED CT
created: 2026-11-22
updated: 2026-11-22
version: 1
status: draft
licence: CC-BY-SA-4.0
copyright: Copyright 2026 Marcus Baw and Baw Medical Ltd. SNOMED CT content © IHTSDO, used under NHS England national licence.
appropriate_use: Identifying whether a patient has a current prescription for one of the 88 medications scored by the ACMI (clincalc's `acmi` calculator), for the purpose of calculating cumulative anticholinergic burden.
misuse: "Not validated for any dose-, route-, or formulation-specific distinction - the ACMI's own model treats any use of these substances as binary. Not a general-purpose anticholinergic medication list - it is exactly the 88 medications in Table 3 of Best et al 2026, no more and no fewer, so it will under-count anticholinergic burden from any medication outside that list."
snomed_release: 2026-09-23
authors:
- name: clincalc (https://github.com/ohtf/clincalc)
  role: author
warnings:
- code: not-universal-definition
  severity: info
  message: This codelist was developed for a specific purpose and may not meet the needs of other studies.
- code: draft-not-reviewed
  severity: info
  message: This codelist has not yet been reviewed. Check status before use.
- code: snomed-release-age
  severity: caution
  message: Validate against the current SNOMED release before use in research.
---

